      "shortDescription": "OHAUS Corporation manufactures weighing, measurement and laboratory equipment. Its official portfolio includes laboratory balances, industrial scales, water-analysis instruments, centrifuges, shakers, mixers, heaters, calibration weights and related accessories.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "Official OHAUS sources trace the company to Gustav and Karl Ohaus, who founded the business in 1907. The current OHAUS Corporation site lists its United States office in Parsippany, New Jersey and presents equipment for laboratory, industrial, education and specialist weighing applications.",
        "The documented product range covers analytical and precision balances, bench, floor, counting and shipping scales, weighing indicators, moisture analysers, water-analysis meters, colorimeters, turbidimeters, laboratory centrifuges, shakers, mixers, heaters and stirrers. OHAUS also publishes reference and calibration weights, test weights, printers and equipment accessories."
      ],
